================
Storm Control Recovery

Why we did this
================
Storm Control protects the network from:

- Broadcast Storms
- Multicast Storms
- Unknown Unicast Storms

When the configured threshold is exceeded, Storm Control may:

- Drop Traffic
- Generate Traps
- Shutdown the Port

While this protects the network, a new problem appears:

After the storm ends, the affected port may remain disabled.

This requires manual intervention by the network administrator.

To reduce downtime and administrative effort, Storm Control Recovery is configured.

It allows ports to automatically recover after a specified period.

What will happen
================
1. Storm Control detects excessive traffic.
2. Port enters Err-Disabled state (if shutdown action is configured).
3. Storm condition ends.
4. Recovery timer starts.
5. Port automatically comes back online.
6. Normal traffic resumes.

Example

During Storm
------------

Broadcast Traffic:
40%

Configured Threshold:
10%

Result:
--------
Port Shutdown


After Storm Ends
----------------

Recovery Timer:
300 Seconds

Result:
--------
Port Automatically Re-enabled

Advantages and Disadvantages of this, hence what came next
==========================================================

Advantages
----------
1. Reduces manual intervention.
2. Improves network availability.
3. Faster service restoration.
4. Reduces operational workload.
5. Works with all Storm Control types.
6. Minimizes downtime.
7. Improves resiliency.

Disadvantages
-------------
1. If root cause still exists, storm may reoccur.
2. Automatic recovery can restore a faulty device.
3. Requires proper timer tuning.
4. May hide recurring network issues.
5. Monitoring is still required.

Hence what came next
--------------------
Even after traffic storms are controlled, administrators still need to secure the switch itself.

Attackers may target:

- Management VLANs
- Management Interfaces
- Administrative Access

To separate management traffic from user traffic, Cisco recommends:

Secure Management VLAN

which provides an isolated VLAN exclusively for switch management.

One-Shot Configuration
======================

Configure Storm Control

Switch(config)# interface fa0/1
Switch(config-if)# storm-control broadcast level 10.00
Switch(config-if)# storm-control action shutdown


Enable Automatic Recovery

Switch(config)# errdisable recovery cause storm-control

Switch(config)# errdisable recovery interval 300

Verification
============

show errdisable recovery

show interfaces status err-disabled

show storm-control

Expected Result
===============

Storm Detected:
---------------
Port Shutdown

Storm Cleared:
--------------
Recovery Timer Starts

Recovery Interval:
------------------
300 Seconds

Port Status:
------------
Automatically Re-enabled

Network Availability:
---------------------
Restored

Summary
=======

Problem:
Storm Control may place a port into Err-Disabled state, requiring manual recovery.

Solution:
Configure Errdisable Recovery for Storm Control events.

Benefit:
Automatically restores normal operation after storm conditions disappear.

Limitation:
Does not fix the original cause of the storm.

